Add this new twitter widget to your sidebar to show your latest tweets.

== Description ==

Add our new twitter widget to your sidebar to show your latest tweets with style and without JavaScript! Retweet, Favorite and Reply links are available.

This twitter widget offer you the possibility to show your last tweet(s) (THE last by default) in your WordPress web site.
The advantage of this twitter plugin is the absence of JavaScript script to load tweets from twitter : a very good point for your page speed.
Another advantage of this newest twitter widget is the possibility to use a cache system with an adjustable period.
You also can show your avatar, action links (Favorite, Reply, Retweet), activate a slideshow of latest tweets, and customize the CSS – everything with this simple twitter plugin.

**Features**

In admin:

* This Twitter Widget is easy to install.
* Panel for easy configuration (Appearance -> Widgets).
* Show or hide your avatar within our Twitter Widget.
* Default CSS can be disabled or customized → Twitter Plugin
* Unlimited customization (colors of the widget, several default styles, etc.)
* Adjustable period for cache system
* Can active the action links
* Can active an auto slideshow script and chose delay between two tweets
* Shortcode to insert the widget where you want
* Included: Tutorial to create a Twitter plugin (needed for API 1.1)

In your site:

* Smart default style (CSS) and compatible with [Social Subscribers Counter](http://wordpress.org/extend/plugins/social-subscribers-counter/) styles
* Flat styles with customizable colors in the Twitter Plugin menu.
* Display link (with special CSS classes) for hastags, users, and web link (`nofollow` links)
* Display twitter's user link and statut's link
* Display source (web, Tweetdeck, etc.) when it's possible within Twitter Plugin Admin Area.
* In option: Show action links like Retweet, Reply and Fav → Twitter Plugin
* In option: little slideshow of one tweet in a list of tweets for this Twitter Plugin

For developpers, numerous hooks are available, template function is available (see FAQ for more info) ;) Just check out the files of our Twitter plugin.

